notes: |
  End-to-end solution architecture for the CI KM capability, in the reference consulting format. Left: real CI knowledge sources from the inventory (Backcast Report SharePoint, regional SharePoints, email chains, MS Teams, OneNote, Planning DB/PIR, Value Opportunity Trackers) with callout 1 automated capture. Feeds column: Graph API connectors, batch crawl, event triggers, manual SME upload. Central zone: ingestion microservices, landing (immutable raw store, event log, lineage), traditional AI/ML (OCR, speech-to-text with diarization, classification, dedup, table extraction), LLM curation as pink overlay callout 2 (template extraction, taxonomy tagging, summarization, entity/relationship extraction, draft confidence scoring, embedding and chunking), SME review queue as human gate callout 4, extraction quality monitoring. Platform zone with banner callout 3: knowledge graph + Profisee metadata as single source of truth; repository, vector + keyword indexes, hybrid retrieval, quality and confidence layer, persistent source links. Access column: faceted search, Q&A assistant with citations and confidence badges, APIs/MCP, subscriptions, usage feedback capture. Consumers: planning and scheduling, backcast and lookback, CI leadership reviews, and dashed future-phase decision-support agents. Dashed feedback loop returns usage signals and SME corrections to curation. Bottom band callout 5: common platform services — governance and lifecycle, quality-tier model, access control and sensitivity, audit and versioning, continuous improvement, monitoring.
